  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Flooding should be abating\n\nRAP and some other meso models do continue to generate some weak\nconvection and bring it into the flood warning areas for the\nnext 3 hrs. We anticipate dropping the flood watch on time since\nwe anticipate no new areas to receive flooding.\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Variable sky conditions for the lunar eclipse \ntonight.\n\nViewing conditions for the lunar eclipse range from fair to \npoor tonight across central PA. It is on-going now per the view\nthrough a few breaks in our local cloud cover. The eclipse is\ntaking place during August's full moon, commonly referred to as\nthe Sturgeon Moon. It will also be the last full moon of the \nsummer with the next full moon set to rise a few nights after \nthe autumnal (Fall) equinox on September 22nd.",
